  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WESTERN PORTLND BIGHT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Portland Bight Protected Area (PBPA) is the largest protected area in Jamaica, and makes up about 10% of the country. Over 100 neotropical migrant species are known to occur in the PBPA, including reddish egret, red knot, white-crowned pigeon, Bicknells thrush, Swainsons warbler, prairie warbler and worm-eating warbler. The principal threat faced by these species is habitat destruction and disturbance, and to a lesser extent illegal hunting. This project will increase support for bird conservation through educational programs at a new conservation center in the PBPA, as well as surrounding communities. The project will also focus on community monitoring and enforcement, and support for development of sustainable ecotourism at the conservation center...</narrative>
  </description>
